@page "/terms"

<PageTitle>Terms | ksamods.gg</PageTitle>

<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated 8 August 2026.</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">What this site is</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                ksamods.gg is an index of mods for Kitten Space Agency. We do not host mod files.
                A listing points at a file in the author's own repository, and we keep the link,
                a hash of the archive we checked, and whatever our validator learned from reading
                it. When you download a mod, you are downloading it from the author, not from us.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
                We are not affiliated with RocketWerkz. Kitten Space Agency is their game.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Installing mods is your risk</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                Code mods are ordinary .NET assemblies. The game loads them into its own process,
                which means they can do anything your user account can do: read your files, open
                network connections, run other programs. Nothing about that is sandboxed.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
                Our validator checks that an archive is packaged the way the game expects. It
                reads the manifest, resolves the declared paths, and records what the mod ships.
                It does not and cannot tell you whether the code inside is safe. A mod passing
                validation is not us vouching for it.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">If you publish here</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                You keep ownership of your work. By listing it you are telling us we can index it
                and show its metadata, and you are confirming you have the right to distribute it
                under the license you picked.
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-muted-foreground">
                <li>Do not publish someone else's work as your own.</li>
                <li>Do not publish anything designed to damage a system or take data from it.</li>
                <li>Keep your listing honest about what the mod does.</li>
                <li>Ids are permanent. Pick one you can live with.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Moderation</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                We can delist anything that breaks the rules above. Delisting removes a mod from
                this index and stops us offering its download. It does not touch the author's
                repository, and it does not reach copies people have already installed. Ids stay
                resolvable after a delisting so modlists that pin them do not silently break.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">No warranty</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                The site is provided as is. We do our best to keep it accurate and available, but
                we cannot promise either, and we are not liable for what a mod does to your game,
                your save files, or your machine. Metadata can be wrong. Links rot. Authors
                delete things.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Changes</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                If these terms change in a way that matters, we will say so on the site rather
                than quietly editing this page. Continuing to use ksamods.gg after a change means
                you accept it.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            @* TODO: contact channel. Needs a real address or invite before launch, since a
               takedown route that does not resolve to a human is not a takedown route. *@
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Getting in touch</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                Problems with a listing, takedown requests, or anything else reach the moderators
                directly. If a listing infringes your work, tell us what it is and what it copies,
                and we will act on it rather than wait for a form.
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
</div>
